### 5.1 Discovery is `git ls-files`-derived, not a filesystem walk

`discover_manifests(repo_root, *, ls_files=None)` obtains its candidate paths by running
`git ls-files -z` at `repo_root` (injectable for tests), filters by basename against the recognized
manifest table, and returns `ManifestRef(path, ecosystem, kind)`.

**Why not a walk.** A walk sees `target/`, `node_modules/`, `.venv/`, `site/` and every gitignored
scratch tree; on this repo that is tens of thousands of vendored manifests, none of which the
project owns. Worse, it sees precisely the class of file the LBS charter §2 warns about — *"noise
against gitignored dev/eval lockfiles"* — and would manufacture a backlog of dependency bumps for
artifacts that do not exist on `main`.

**The tracked manifest set at `cbb56212` — 28 paths, enumerated.** Reproduce with:

```bash
git ls-files | grep -E '(^|/)(Cargo\.toml|Cargo\.lock|package\.json|package-lock\.json|pyproject\.toml|uv\.lock|requirements[^/]*\.txt|setup\.py)$'
```

| Path | Ecosystem | Kind | Disposition |
|---|---|---|---|
| `Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `Cargo.lock` | cargo | lockfile | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb-cli/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb-embedder/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb-embedder-api/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb-engine/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb-napi/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb-py/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb-query/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/rust/crates/fathomdb-schema/Cargo.toml` | cargo | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/python/pyproject.toml` | pypi | manifest | `shipped` |
| `src/python/uv.lock` | pypi | lockfile | `shipped` |
