  When Slice 32 implements this, `TierMap.classify()` can be data-driven here while `run_survey()` still hardcodes `path.startswith("dev/release/fixtures/")` and passes both AC-SBOM-05 and this test. That leaves REQ-5's “never by a hardcoded special case in code” untested at the actual survey boundary; the stripped tier map needs to be passed into the survey path/CLI and shown to make fixture manifests fail tiering instead of being excluded.

